From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: chipidea: qcom: treat MDM9607 as fixed peripheral

MDM9607 advertises both host and device capabilities, so ChipIdea marks the
controller as OTG even when the board DT fixes dr_mode to peripheral.  The
forced-VBUS path is only consulted for a non-OTG controller.  Consequently
vbus_active remains clear and binding a gadget never invokes either the
controller-reset or pull-up notification.

Mark MDM9607 as dual-role hardware without an OTG role. This makes the
existing fixed-peripheral VBUS flag effective while retaining the
peripheral-only DT and build configuration.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
@@ -310,8 +310,15 @@ static int ci_hdrc_msm_probe(struct plat
 	ci->force_peripheral_session =
 		of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
 					"qcom,mdm9607-ci-hdrc");
+	/*
+	 * The core advertises both host and device capabilities, but this
+	 * board path is wired and described as peripheral-only. Without
+	 * DUAL_ROLE_NOT_OTG, ci_handle_vbus_change() ignores the forced VBUS
+	 * state and waits for OTGSC.BSV forever.
+	 */
 	if (ci->force_peripheral_session)
-		ci->pdata.flags |= CI_HDRC_FORCE_VBUS_ACTIVE_ALWAYS;
+		ci->pdata.flags |= CI_HDRC_DUAL_ROLE_NOT_OTG |
+				  CI_HDRC_FORCE_VBUS_ACTIVE_ALWAYS;
 
 	ci->pdata.notify_event = ci_hdrc_msm_notify_event;
 
